INPUT:
  - part_number (str)
  - quantity (int)

PROCESSING:
  - Get part number and quantity from user.
  - Match part against cost configuration using string comparison logic:
      - "10" or "55" -> cost = $1.00
      - "99"         -> cost = $2.00
      - "80" or "70" -> cost = $3.00
      - All others   -> cost = $5.00
  - Calculate total cost = quantity * unit cost

OUTPUT:
  - part_number (str)
  - unit_cost (float)   [Decimals aligned]
  - total_cost (float)  [Decimals aligned]
